<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dutch</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Dutch are the people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, who became a leading maritime and commercial power in the seventeenth century. Through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a> and its trading companies they competed with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>, traded with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa Shogunate</a>, and dealt with African states such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Ashanti Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin Empire</a>.</p></div>
